      "language": "Solidity",
      "description": "Attackers exploited an accounting discrepancy in K3 Capital's sBOLD vault that excluded WETH collateral below a configured threshold from share valuations. Using flash-loaned capital, they minted sBOLD shares while the collateral was undervalued, triggered swaps that converted the uncounted collateral into BOLD, and redeemed their shares at the increased valuation. Repeating this process across 97 transactions drained approximately $3.42M in BOLD from the vault."
